    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "collStats.freeStorageSize reports storage available for reuse. The scale argument changes its units, and the documented field can be absent when no storage is available for reuse. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ef712c0dfa072d2ac0b853740746ec5d773d3bfa4faf315bcc1a384051ea6c79",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:311562b156f1dd8fa2fc86549fd9aa7216349c3779178893f4c311acd1c7c495"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Compaction is a best-effort process and does not guarantee a reduction in file size. Whether space is released depends on how many blocks are available to release and their location in the data file; for example, the checkpoint written after a compaction pass can land at the end of the file and prevent truncation. Sources: https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
          "source": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4b310b9ae002ee092942224cc2f1ff90c9bcbd64c387b198616971589912c1a4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
