    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Dropping a collection or index releases the disk space occupied by that object, unlike deleting individual documents while retaining the object's files. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8b870098468668e595566362f5e61f7bc3d9d33434e503b5e480fdecc7bd17a0",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a7a23a4cb1b4680117a31ff38ea860e3bde995bdeec439d5a2321ab083f466ea"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Deleting documents leaves space inside WiredTiger data files available for later reuse; it does not generally return those bytes to the operating system. Logical data reduction therefore need not reduce filesystem usage. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ef3b0c57f8a6a5b332f6ba84985ab38f8e553419e996ea00c51c8aab974c771a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a7a23a4cb1b4680117a31ff38ea860e3bde995bdeec439d5a2321ab083f466ea"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage",
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The wiredTiger.block-manager statistic named \"file bytes available for reuse\" measures internal reusable space in bytes; it is not a measurement of filesystem free capacity. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6c83612a6391d00c2b576c9cab2936ff2340cb1569afb1e6ebe980a8e60ad586",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:38446b619cd2561ae5ba8d8c61bd58eb136c22930257c32186a2c93626ee19a2",
            "ev:a7a23a4cb1b4680117a31ff38ea860e3bde995bdeec439d5a2321ab083f466ea"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/",
            "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "storageSize includes allocated collection storage, including unused allocation, and reflects compression; it excludes indexes. totalSize adds totalIndexSize. Comparing logical size directly with storageSize is therefore not a reliable measure of WiredTiger free blocks. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:21e50e5b47f511e8565f7772afae65f7710c031eeebb7e0fcd44f99bc258d9bb",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4cc1912b860a1d8a064da6ebec0e3e1210e3a1e8739aad87213c72368790421c",
            "ev:72e6a7436da99a532e54dd6a77a63b207daaf5a896fd5e11434c0faaae36ab58",
            "ev:923479c15c19883915720c5c7618fb3d845eae26f35283ea5b4e3f9f76dc8ed2"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "WiredTiger retains blocks referenced by checkpoints. Replacing a page does not make its previous disk block reusable until the checkpoint referencing that block has been removed and checkpoint metadata has been resolved. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ce421e46c1bda50964cc331ea7e5c202d9c20716125f126eb68d19ccdf873ac9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6",
            "ev:ad05ab9d33ff9bc2eda8388efe0a5d007b226bab11acf48e18e90d701d49df83",
            "ev:ff18a08a1a76836c2e4ca3d431d61cac44e0c41d03638e6359aa2f3da9f59f9a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/wiki/Block-Manager-Overview"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Compaction can move live blocks from a file's end into reusable blocks near its beginning, then truncate the free tail. Interior holes are therefore potential relocation destinations, even though truncation itself occurs at the file end. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6140b4c05a4dae5fdc4ef4cccc5cc450773fa8cbc9eb04be4ba994fd23624b83",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
            "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/wiki/Block-Manager-Overview"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Measure collection statistics with collStats before and after compaction. compact attempts to release obsolete blocks to the operating system, and its effectiveness depends on how many blocks are available to release and their location in the data file. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:856e9035c7f5a27212d1b066af4f42a2acb5837e82c3455bca76765bde93791b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:255f14287ea6b68d5721d64b469641be61acfc35c84955b47e5d0ccc5647d2ac",
            "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "claim_id": "clm:90fd689a1ea892f9872d14683c642642218dd2208e43ef5722a829088f363171",
            "outcome": "CORRECTED",
            "at": "2026-11-02T13:06:46Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "A compact operation covers both collection data and its associated indexes. A collection-only reusable-space statistic should not be treated as a complete prediction of the total bytes the operation will free. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:42f6fba1b3fb23351125e21a5dde99ee84c999e5248f27e42ec4f47ba2b06f85",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc",
            "ev:72e6a7436da99a532e54dd6a77a63b207daaf5a896fd5e11434c0faaae36ab58",
            "ev:923479c15c19883915720c5c7618fb3d845eae26f35283ea5b4e3f9f76dc8ed2"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Percona's published PSMDB 6.0.14 experiment reported 306188288 reusable collection bytes before compaction, 34000896 afterward, and bytesFreed of 507662336 while inserts continued. These observations are a workload-specific example, not a universal conversion from reusable bytes to returned disk space. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:51b6d34fdaffbdb1dd4d2959576f6afd827921dfc4cf924988224cca7c51b3c9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:71737ac37753278967989fc27c1d2364ba4dcd7b889fdcf8713e36c75f11af22"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "collStats.freeStorageSize reports the amount of storage available for reuse. compact attempts to release obsolete blocks to the operating system, but its effectiveness depends on how many blocks are available to release and their location in the data file, so freeStorageSize is not a guarantee of bytes returned. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:60b6999e3a51aa7dea384a79cb1483f2d911edc0faffdaea81c8b0e56f07b0dc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
